  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "ISS04 confinement enhancement factor H_ISS04 = 1.4 sustained in a quasi-axisymmetric (QA) stellarator — never experimentally demonstrated in QA geometry (only achieved in W7-X's QI configuration)",
      "324-coil software-controlled planar REBCO array scales reliably from 9-coil Canis prototype to full power plant with 450+ independent control variables",
      "Novel non-resonant toroidally continuous X-point divertor for QA stellarator delivers 10× better neutral compression than island divertors (simulation-only claim)",
      "Helium impingement jet cooling of 51,000 hexagonal tungsten tiles handles 10 MW/m² steady-state heat flux in stellarator geometry",
      "LiPb breeding blanket with EUROFER97 structure and SiC MHD inserts achieves TBR ≥ 1.1 (idealized 1.3) under 14 MeV neutron flux at plant throughput",
      "Sector-based remote maintenance enables 84-day biennial replacement cycle supporting 88% capacity factor",
      "V-4Cr-4Ti vanadium alloy first wall survives 15 full-power years and can be manufactured at multi-hundred-tonne scale"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "Continuous current drive system (LHCD/ECRH) — Helios is effectively ignited with only 1 MW operational ECRH for impurity control, eliminating the recirculating power penalty of pulsed/current-drive tokamaks",
      "Disruption mitigation systems and disruption-induced damage repair — steady-state stellarator operation has no disruption risk",
      "Complex 3D coil manufacturing — planar coil geometry is simpler to wind and mass-producible compared to conventional 3D stellarator coils or compact tokamak demountable coils",
      "Port-restricted remote maintenance infrastructure — sector-based removal eliminates ITER-style port access constraints"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "336 individually addressable REBCO coil circuits (12 encircling + 324 shaping) each requiring dedicated power supply, cryogenic cooling, and control infrastructure",
      "Software/controls infrastructure for real-time management of 450+ independent control variables in a burning plasma",
      "V-4Cr-4Ti (V44) nuclear-grade vanadium alloy first wall — never produced at multi-hundred-tonne scale, requires premium purification from commodity vanadium",
      "Novel QA X-point divertor with helium impingement jet cooling of 51,000 hexagonal tungsten tiles — no design-validated analogue in any existing facility",
      "65% Li-6 enriched LiPb inventory (~2.7M kg estimated) requiring Western alternative to mercury-based enrichment process"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "ISS04 H=1.4 confinement enhancement unvalidated in QA geometry; if operational H_ISS04 is 1.2, fusion power could drop 30–50%, requiring larger machine or accepting reduced output",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Novel QA X-point divertor at TRL 1–2 with no experimental precedent; underperformance would compromise impurity control, fuel purity, and first-wall lifetime",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "No published bottom-up capital cost breakdown — $150/MWh FOAK and $60/MWh NOAK targets are asserted without supporting cost model; magnet system is likely dominant but unquantified",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "324 individually controlled coil circuits create novel single-point failure modes (power supplies, cryo circuits, control software) that could reduce 88% capacity factor target",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "V-4Cr-4Ti first wall material has never been produced at multi-hundred-tonne nuclear-grade scale; substitution would cascade into activation inventory and remote handling changes",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "6.6% alpha particle loss (~12.7 MW deposited on first wall/divertor) higher than tokamak typical 2–4%, increasing materials endurance burden beyond 15-year first-wall lifetime assumption",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "EUROFER97 structural performance at 150+ dpa unvalidated until IFMIF-DONES operates (early 2030s); current data only to ~15 dpa from fission reactors",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "65% Li-6 enrichment supply chain concentrated in Russia/China (mercury process banned in West); Western alternative process still under development",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "REBCO tape demand at thousands to tens-of-thousands of km exceeds current global production capacity; price must drop from $30–100/kA-m to ~$10/kA-m for commercial viability",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tritium extraction efficiency from LiPb at plant throughput unvalidated anywhere; loss rates above 1% per cycle would compromise breeding self-sufficiency",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Sector-based remote maintenance scheme has not been prototyped for any fusion device; 84-day window achievability at plant scale unproven",
        "severity": "low"
      },
      {
        "description": "Helium coolant system (blowers, manifolds, IHX) less mature than equivalent water/steam systems; tritium permeation through helium-to-water heat exchangers unmanaged at plant scale",
        "severity": "low"
      }
